Singleton Design Pattern : 

    The goal of using this pattern is to make sure we can only create a single object of this class in our entire application. 

    We typically make our class to be a singleton class when the expense of creating object is very high or there isn't any attribute difference between multiple instances of the class. 

    When we want to centralise logic or control, example storing of cache across the application. 

There different variations of singleton class each will be explained in detail and its use cases and its technical tradeoffs. 



First to understand more about creating object and its pattern, what is the core component of class that is responsible for the creation of object ?? 

Constructor ! If we want to limit the object first we should make sure that constructor is not accessible to the outside world. 

Refer to the different code blocks effectively explaining popular variations of singleton design principle.